.SS "\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP createGear (\fBPhysicsBody\fP other, number ratio, number phase = \fR0\fP)"

.PP
Couple rotations at a fixed ratio\&. Maintains other\&.rotation * ratio - this\&.rotation = phase\&. Requires two distinct instantiated bodies in the same world\&. Anchors are unscaled body-local coordinates, independent of artwork scaling\&. Basic and Chipmunk implement the same relationship with different numerical trajectories\&. Endpoints own the active handle; native callers must retain it explicitly to use it after disconnection\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIother\fP Other instantiated \fBPhysicsBody\fP; may belong to a \fBSprite\fP or \fBPart\fP\&. 
.br
\fIratio\fP Finite nonzero signed ratio\&. 
.br
\fIphase\fP Finite angular phase in radians; default zero\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The new \fBPhysicsConstraint\fP handle\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP createGrooveJoint (\fBPhysicsBody\fP other, \fBPoint\fP start, \fBPoint\fP end, \fBPoint\fP otherAnchor)"

.PP
Slide an anchor along a segment on this body\&. Motion along the segment remains free; its endpoints limit travel\&. Requires two distinct instantiated bodies in the same world\&. Anchors are unscaled body-local coordinates, independent of artwork scaling\&. Basic and Chipmunk implement the same relationship with different numerical trajectories\&. Endpoints own the active handle; native callers must retain it explicitly to use it after disconnection\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIother\fP Other instantiated \fBPhysicsBody\fP; may belong to a \fBSprite\fP or \fBPart\fP\&. 
.br
\fIstart\fP Finite segment start in this body’s local coordinates\&. 
.br
\fIend\fP Finite distinct segment end in this body’s local coordinates\&. 
.br
\fIotherAnchor\fP Anchor in the other body’s local distance coordinates; default origin where optional\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The new \fBPhysicsConstraint\fP handle\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP createMotor (\fBPhysicsBody\fP other, number radiansPerSecond, number maxTorque)"

.PP
Drive a relative angular speed with a torque limit\&. Positive speed turns B clockwise relative to A\&. Requires two distinct instantiated bodies in the same world\&. Anchors are unscaled body-local coordinates, independent of artwork scaling\&. Basic and Chipmunk implement the same relationship with different numerical trajectories\&. Endpoints own the active handle; native callers must retain it explicitly to use it after disconnection\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIother\fP Other instantiated \fBPhysicsBody\fP; may belong to a \fBSprite\fP or \fBPart\fP\&. 
.br
\fIradiansPerSecond\fP Finite target B-minus-A angular speed, in radians/second\&. 
.br
\fImaxTorque\fP Finite nonnegative maximum torque\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The new \fBPhysicsConstraint\fP handle\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP createPinJoint (\fBPhysicsBody\fP other, \fBPoint\fP anchor = \fR\fBPoint\fP(0,0)\fP, \fBPoint\fP otherAnchor = \fR\fBPoint\fP(0,0)\fP)"

.PP
Preserve the initial distance between two anchors\&. Captures distance at creation\&. Coincident anchors behave as a pivot\&. Requires two distinct instantiated bodies in the same world\&. Anchors are unscaled body-local coordinates, independent of artwork scaling\&. Basic and Chipmunk implement the same relationship with different numerical trajectories\&. Endpoints own the active handle; native callers must retain it explicitly to use it after disconnection\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIother\fP Other instantiated \fBPhysicsBody\fP; may belong to a \fBSprite\fP or \fBPart\fP\&. 
.br
\fIanchor\fP Anchor in this body’s local distance coordinates; default origin where optional\&. 
.br
\fIotherAnchor\fP Anchor in the other body’s local distance coordinates; default origin where optional\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The new \fBPhysicsConstraint\fP handle\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP createPivotJoint (\fBPhysicsBody\fP other, \fBPoint\fP anchor = \fR\fBPoint\fP(0,0)\fP, \fBPoint\fP otherAnchor = \fR\fBPoint\fP(0,0)\fP)"

.PP
Keep two body-local anchors coincident\&. The two anchors need not initially coincide\&. Requires two distinct instantiated bodies in the same world\&. Anchors are unscaled body-local coordinates, independent of artwork scaling\&. Basic and Chipmunk implement the same relationship with different numerical trajectories\&. Endpoints own the active handle; native callers must retain it explicitly to use it after disconnection\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIother\fP Other instantiated \fBPhysicsBody\fP; may belong to a \fBSprite\fP or \fBPart\fP\&. 
.br
\fIanchor\fP Anchor in this body’s local distance coordinates; default origin where optional\&. 
.br
\fIotherAnchor\fP Anchor in the other body’s local distance coordinates; default origin where optional\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The new \fBPhysicsConstraint\fP handle\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP createRatchet (\fBPhysicsBody\fP other, number interval, number phase = \fR0\fP)"

.PP
Permit rotation through discrete one-way teeth\&. Positive interval permits increasing B-minus-A rotation; negative interval reverses the direction\&. Requires two distinct instantiated bodies in the same world\&. Anchors are unscaled body-local coordinates, independent of artwork scaling\&. Basic and Chipmunk implement the same relationship with different numerical trajectories\&. Endpoints own the active handle; native callers must retain it explicitly to use it after disconnection\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIother\fP Other instantiated \fBPhysicsBody\fP; may belong to a \fBSprite\fP or \fBPart\fP\&. 
.br
\fIinterval\fP Finite nonzero signed tooth interval in radians\&. 
.br
\fIphase\fP Finite angular tooth offset in radians; default zero\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The new \fBPhysicsConstraint\fP handle\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP createRotaryLimit (\fBPhysicsBody\fP other, number minAngle, number maxAngle)"

.PP
Limit the relative angle of two bodies\&. Limits apply to B rotation minus A rotation, in unwrapped radians\&. Requires two distinct instantiated bodies in the same world\&. Anchors are unscaled body-local coordinates, independent of artwork scaling\&. Basic and Chipmunk implement the same relationship with different numerical trajectories\&. Endpoints own the active handle; native callers must retain it explicitly to use it after disconnection\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIother\fP Other instantiated \fBPhysicsBody\fP; may belong to a \fBSprite\fP or \fBPart\fP\&. 
.br
\fIminAngle\fP Finite minimum clockwise relative angle\&. 
.br
\fImaxAngle\fP Finite maximum angle, at least the minimum\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The new \fBPhysicsConstraint\fP handle\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP createRotarySpring (\fBPhysicsBody\fP other, number restAngle, number stiffness, number damping)"

.PP
Join rotations with a damped torsional spring\&. Rest angle is body B rotation minus body A rotation, clockwise positive\&. Requires two distinct instantiated bodies in the same world\&. Anchors are unscaled body-local coordinates, independent of artwork scaling\&. Basic and Chipmunk implement the same relationship with different numerical trajectories\&. Endpoints own the active handle; native callers must retain it explicitly to use it after disconnection\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIother\fP Other instantiated \fBPhysicsBody\fP; may belong to a \fBSprite\fP or \fBPart\fP\&. 
.br
\fIrestAngle\fP Finite rest angle in radians\&. 
.br
\fIstiffness\fP Finite nonnegative torque per radian\&. 
.br
\fIdamping\fP Finite nonnegative torque per radian/second\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The new \fBPhysicsConstraint\fP handle\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP createSlideJoint (\fBPhysicsBody\fP other, \fBPoint\fP anchor, \fBPoint\fP otherAnchor, number minDistance, number maxDistance)"

.PP
Limit the separation of two anchors\&. The anchors move freely between the limits\&. Requires two distinct instantiated bodies in the same world\&. Anchors are unscaled body-local coordinates, independent of artwork scaling\&. Basic and Chipmunk implement the same relationship with different numerical trajectories\&. Endpoints own the active handle; native callers must retain it explicitly to use it after disconnection\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIother\fP Other instantiated \fBPhysicsBody\fP; may belong to a \fBSprite\fP or \fBPart\fP\&. 
.br
\fIanchor\fP Anchor in this body’s local distance coordinates; default origin where optional\&. 
.br
\fIotherAnchor\fP Anchor in the other body’s local distance coordinates; default origin where optional\&. 
.br
\fIminDistance\fP Finite nonnegative minimum distance\&. 
.br
\fImaxDistance\fP Finite maximum distance, at least the minimum\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The new \fBPhysicsConstraint\fP handle\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP createSpring (\fBPhysicsBody\fP other, \fBPoint\fP anchor, \fBPoint\fP otherAnchor, number restLength, number stiffness, number damping)"

.PP
Join anchors with a damped linear spring\&. Pulls or pushes toward the rest length\&. Requires two distinct instantiated bodies in the same world\&. Anchors are unscaled body-local coordinates, independent of artwork scaling\&. Basic and Chipmunk implement the same relationship with different numerical trajectories\&. Endpoints own the active handle; native callers must retain it explicitly to use it after disconnection\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIother\fP Other instantiated \fBPhysicsBody\fP; may belong to a \fBSprite\fP or \fBPart\fP\&. 
.br
\fIanchor\fP Anchor in this body’s local distance coordinates; default origin where optional\&. 
.br
\fIotherAnchor\fP Anchor in the other body’s local distance coordinates; default origin where optional\&. 
.br
\fIrestLength\fP Finite nonnegative rest length\&. 
.br
\fIstiffness\fP Finite nonnegative force per distance unit\&. 
.br
\fIdamping\fP Finite nonnegative force per unit relative speed\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The new \fBPhysicsConstraint\fP handle\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsBody\fP disconnect (\fBPhysicsBody\fP other = \fRnull\fP)"

.PP
Disconnect this body’s constraints\&. Retained constraint handles remain safe and report NoPhysics endpoints\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIother\fP Optional other endpoint; omission or null disconnects all\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "number getAngularDamping ()"

.PP
Read the body's angular damping\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The current angular damping\&. Returns zero for NoPhysics\&. Units are inverse seconds\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetAngularDamping()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "number getAngularMomentum ()"

.PP
Read rotational momentum\&. For an active \fBSprite\fP rig, sum component spin and orbital momentum about the assembly center of mass: \fRsum(I_i * omega_i + m_i * cross(r_i - COM, v_i - VCOM))\fP\&. This includes attached Kinematic bodies, excludes the coordinating body and unregistered/detached parts, and does not assume all parts rotate together\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Signed clockwise angular momentum in mass times distance squared per second\&. For a single body, moment of inertia multiplied by angular velocity\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetMomentOfInertia()\fP, \fBgetAngularVelocity()\fP, \fBapplyAngularImpulse()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "number getAngularVelocity ()"

.PP
Read the body's angular velocity\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The current angular velocity\&. Returns zero for NoPhysics\&. Units are clockwise radians per second\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetAngularVelocity()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "number getBreakAngularSpeed ()"

.PP
Read the configured angular-speed threshold\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The threshold in radians/second; zero means disabled, including NoPhysics\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetBreakAngularSpeed()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsBody\fP getBreakAngularSpeedReference ()"

.PP
Read the optional angular-speed reference body\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The borrowed reference body, or null for absolute speed or disabled monitoring\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetBreakAngularSpeed()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP getConstraint (uint index)"

.PP
Read a connected constraint by list index\&. Indices shift after disconnection\&. Out-of-range indices throw\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIindex\fP Zero-based index into this body’s current connections\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Borrowed native reference to the shared constraint; JavaScript retains the handle\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "number getConstraintCount ()"

.PP
Count connected constraints on this body\&. The same constraint appears on both endpoint bodies\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Number of active connections; zero for NoPhysics\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "object getDriveState ()"

.PP
Copy the drive target, last actuation and current target error\&. Returns an independent snapshot\&. When disabled, enabled is false and numeric fields are zero\&. Reading never creates a body or emits a NoPhysics warning\&.

.PP

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A plain object with the fields above\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetDriveTarget()\fP, \fBisDriveEnabled()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "number getFriction ()"

.PP
Read the body's contact friction\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The current contact friction\&. Returns zero for NoPhysics\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetFriction()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "number getLinearDamping ()"

.PP
Read the body's linear damping\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The current linear damping\&. Returns zero for NoPhysics\&. Units are inverse seconds\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetLinearDamping()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "number getMass ()"

.PP
Read the body's mass\&. For a \fBSprite\fP with an active explicit or generated animation physics rig, this is the sum of registered component masses, including Kinematic components; unrelated and detached Parts are excluded\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The current mass\&. Returns zero for NoPhysics\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetMass()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "number getMode ()"

.PP
Read the body's simulation mode\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The current simulation mode\&. Returns \fBpdg\&.physicsBody_None\fP for NoPhysics\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetMode()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "number getMomentOfInertia ()"

.PP
Read the body's moment of inertia\&. For an active \fBSprite\fP rig, return the instantaneous inertia about its center of mass: \fRsum(I_i + m_i * distanceSquared(r_i, COM))\fP\&. This is the inertia the current pose would have if locked rigidly; it changes as articulated parts move\&. It counts exactly the same attached components as \fBgetMass()\fP, including Kinematic bodies\&. The coordinating body's saved single-body inertia is not included\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The current moment of inertia in mass times distance squared\&. Returns zero for NoPhysics\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetMomentOfInertia()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "number getMovementDirectionInRadians ()"

.PP
Read the direction of linear velocity\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
atan2(velocity\&.y, velocity\&.x), in radians\&. Zero points along positive x; positive angles turn clockwise\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetVelocityInRadians()\fP, \fBgetSpeed()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "number getRestitution ()"

.PP
Read the body's restitution\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The current restitution\&. Returns zero for NoPhysics\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetRestitution()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "number getSolver ()"

.PP
Identify the active physics solver\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
\fR\fBpdg\&.physicsSolver_None\fP\fP for NoPhysics, \fR\fBpdg\&.physicsSolver_Basic\fP\fP for the analytic integrator, or \fR\fBpdg\&.physicsSolver_Chipmunk\fP\fP for a layer-owned solver\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBisPresent()\fP, \fBstep()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "number getSpeed ()"

.PP
Read the body's speed\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The current speed\&. Returns zero for NoPhysics\&. Units are distance per second\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetSpeed()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "object getState ()"

.PP
Copy the current physical state\&. Reads the active solver when one is attached\&. Changing the returned object does not change the body\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
An owned object with the fields below\&.
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBPhysics state\fP
.RS 4
Field  Meaning  \fRx\fP, \fRy\fP  Center position in owning-layer distance units\&.  \fRrotation\fP  Clockwise angle in radians\&.  \fRvelocityX\fP, \fRvelocityY\fP  Linear velocity in distance units per second\&.  \fRangularVelocity\fP  Clockwise angular velocity in radians per second\&.  
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBteleport()\fP, \fBsetVelocity()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBVector\fP getVelocity ()"

.PP
Read linear velocity\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A new \fBVector\fP in owning-layer distance units per second\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetVelocity()\fP, \fBgetSpeed()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "boolean isAttached ()"

.PP
Test whether an owner publishes this body's motion\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True while associated with a \fBSprite\fP or \fBPart\fP\&. False after removal; a retained detached body remains usable\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBstep()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "boolean isDriveEnabled ()"

.PP
Test whether a physical drive is enabled\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True while a drive is installed, including when its target is blocked or already reached\&. False for NoPhysics\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetDriveState()\fP, \fBclearDrive()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "boolean isPresent ()"

.PP
Test whether this is a real physics body\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
False for the shared NoPhysics object; true for a body created explicitly\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetMode()\fP, \fBisAttached()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "boolean removeForce (uint id)"

.PP
Cancel a force or torque registration\&. Works for pending, finite, and continuous loads\&. Removing an expired or unknown ID is harmless\&.

.PP
For active \fBSprite\fP rigs, see \fBphysics_assembly_loads\fP\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIid\fP The ID returned when the force or torque was registered\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True if a pending/active load was removed; false otherwise\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBapplyForce()\fP, \fBapplyTorque()\fP, \fBstopAllForces()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsBody\fP setAngularDamping (number value)"

.PP
Set the body's angular damping\&. Damping slows angular velocity over time; it is separate from contact friction\&. Invalid values throw on a present body\&. NoPhysics ignores the operation\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvalue\fP Finite nonnegative exponential damping rate per second\&. Zero disables damping\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetAngularDamping()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsBody\fP setAngularVelocity (number value)"

.PP
Set the body's angular velocity\&. Static bodies retain zero angular velocity\&. Invalid values throw on a present body\&. NoPhysics ignores the operation\&.

.PP
A rigidly mounted \fBSprite\fP's body rejects this operation; animate its mounting \fBPart\fP or detach it first\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvalue\fP Finite angular velocity in radians per second; positive is clockwise\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetAngularVelocity()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsBody\fP setBreakAngularSpeed (number radiansPerSecond)"

.PP
Notify when absolute angular speed exceeds the limit\&. This selects absolute angular speed and clears any previous reference body\&. See the reference-body overload for sampling, rearming, events and snapshots\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIradiansPerSecond\fP Finite nonnegative radians/second; zero disables\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBPhysicsBody\fP, for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetBreakAngularSpeed(number, PhysicsBody)\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsBody\fP setBreakAngularSpeed (number radiansPerSecond, \fBPhysicsBody\fP referenceBody)"

.PP
Notify when a body exceeds an angular-speed threshold\&. The threshold is a notification condition, not a speed clamp\&. It does not apply braking, disconnect constraints, or split artwork\&. Existing motor and force-break behavior is unchanged\&. Both basic and Chipmunk solvers support it, including kinematic bodies and bodies without a collider or joint\&.

.PP
A positive-duration physics step compares the magnitude of the solved angular velocity against the threshold\&. Equality does not trigger an event\&. One event is sent per excursion above the limit; a later sampled speed at or below the limit rearms it\&. Sampling occurs after each world step (before restoring temporary Chipmunk kinematic sweep velocities), or after \fBstep()\fP for a detached basic body\&. It does not detect peaks between those samples\&. Setters and zero-duration steps never dispatch events synchronously\&.

.PP
Changing the threshold or reference rearms monitoring\&. Repeating the same settings preserves the notification state\&. Invalid edits throw without changing settings or rearming\&. Zero disables monitoring and clears the reference\&. NoPhysics ignores this operation and always reports zero\&.

.PP
With a reference, speed means \fRabs(body\&.angularVelocity - referenceBody\&.angularVelocity)\fP; otherwise it means \fRabs(body\&.angularVelocity)\fP\&. The reference must be a different present body in the same \fBSpriteLayer\fP, or both bodies must be outside a layer\&. The association is weak: removing its body from its owner or destroying it disables dependent monitors\&. A world mismatch detected at sampling also disables the monitor\&. A detached body retains its absolute threshold; relative monitoring is cleared on detachment\&.

.PP
\fBSprite\fP bodies emit eventType_SpriteBreak on their \fBSprite\fP; \fBPart\fP bodies emit it on the owning \fBSprite\fP with the \fBPart\fP identified\&. Returning false leaves the body and joints unchanged\&. Snapshots preserve settings and the notification latch\&. Relative references require a Sprite/Layer graph containing both bodies; external references are rejected\&. Event handlers are not saved\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIradiansPerSecond\fP Finite nonnegative magnitude in radians/second\&. Default body setting is zero (disabled)\&. 
.br
\fIreferenceBody\fP Optional borrowed reference body; omitted, null or undefined selects absolute speed\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBPhysicsBody\fP, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The example assumes \fBSprite\fP objects named sprite and housing in the same layer\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const shaft = sprite\&.setupPhysicsBody();
shaft\&.setBreakAngularSpeed(3000 * 2 * Math\&.PI / 60); // 3,000 RPM
sprite\&.addHandler(new pdg\&.IEventHandler(function(event) {
    if (event\&.reason === pdg\&.physicsBreak_AngularSpeed) {
        console\&.log('Shaft overspeed:', event\&.angularSpeed);
        // Decide which attachments to release in your game\&.
    }
    return true;
}), pdg\&.eventType_SpriteBreak);
// Or measure relative to a housing body in the same layer:
shaft\&.setBreakAngularSpeed(100, housing\&.setupPhysicsBody());

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetBreakAngularSpeed()\fP, \fBgetBreakAngularSpeedReference()\fP, \fBSpriteBreakEvent\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsBody\fP setDriveTarget (\fBPoint\fP position, number radians, number maxForce, number maxTorque, number frequency = \fR4\fP, number dampingRatio = \fR1\fP, int direction = \fR\fBrotationDirection_Shortest\fP\fP)"

.PP
Drive a dynamic body toward a position and orientation using bounded force and torque\&. Installs or replaces an active spring/damper target\&. The operation preserves the current position and velocity\&. Each physics step adds a drive contribution to other applied loads; collisions and constraints still determine the solved pose\&. Repeated successful manual \fBsetDriveTarget()\fP calls replace the same manual target; the last call wins\&. Invalid updates preserve the previous target\&. A blocked or force-limited body may never reach its target\&. The drive stays enabled until \fBclearDrive()\fP, \fBstopAllForces()\fP, or a change to kinematic/static mode\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIposition\fP Target in owning-layer coordinates; a detached body uses its world frame\&. 
.br
\fIradians\fP Target orientation in radians, positive clockwise\&. 
.br
\fImaxForce\fP Finite nonnegative limit on the magnitude of the linear drive force, in mass units times distance units per second squared\&. Zero disables translation actuation\&. 
.br
\fImaxTorque\fP Finite nonnegative angular drive torque limit, in inertia units times radians per second squared\&. Zero disables angular actuation\&. 
.br
\fIfrequency\fP Finite positive response frequency in cycles per second; default 4\&. Larger values request faster correction, subject to the force limits\&. 
.br
\fIdampingRatio\fP Finite nonnegative damping ratio; default 1 requests critical damping in the unconstrained linear model\&. Zero permits oscillation\&. 
.br
\fIdirection\fP Integer rotationDirection constant; default rotationDirection_Shortest\&. Clockwise/CounterClockwise select a signed route at assignment\&. AsSpecified retains the unwrapped target, including full turns\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBPhysicsBody\fP\&. NoPhysics returns the shared singleton without storing a target\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Requires a dynamic body\&. Invalid numeric values, unsupported direction constants, or competing rigid-mount ownership throw before changing the target\&. Limits bound only the drive contribution; independent impulses, forces, gravity and constraint responses can produce additional motion\&. The basic solver uses bounded spring/damper integration, while Chipmunk applies the drive before its shared contact/constraint solve\&. Numerical trajectories need not match exactly\&.
.RE
.PP
.PP
.nf
const body = sprite\&.setupPhysicsBody(2, 4);
body\&.setDriveTarget(new pdg\&.Point(120, 80), 0\&.5, 40, 12, 3, 1,
                    pdg\&.rotationDirection_Shortest);
// The Sprite/Part world advances its body\&. Query whether the goal is still blocked:
const remaining = body\&.getDriveState()\&.positionError;
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Rig tracking and \fBPart\fP IK controllers reserve their participating drives\&. Release rig tracking with Sprite::setAnimationPhysicsMode(animationPhysics_Dynamic)\&. Call \fBPart::clearIKTarget()\fP to release a \fBPart\fP IK chain before replacing or clearing such a drive, stopping all forces, or changing away from dynamic mode\&. Independent impulses and forces remain available\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetDriveState()\fP, \fBclearDrive()\fP, \fBsetMode()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
References \fBpdg::rotationDirection_Shortest\fP\&.
.SS "\fBPhysicsBody\fP setFriction (number value)"

.PP
Set the body's contact friction\&. Affects contacts, not free-motion damping\&. \fBSprite\fP and \fBPart\fP collider shapes use this material unless they override it\&. Invalid values throw on a present body\&. NoPhysics ignores the operation\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvalue\fP Finite nonnegative friction coefficient\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetFriction()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsBody\fP setLinearDamping (number value)"

.PP
Set the body's linear damping\&. Damping slows velocity over time; it is separate from contact friction\&. Invalid values throw on a present body\&. NoPhysics ignores the operation\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvalue\fP Finite nonnegative exponential damping rate per second\&. Zero disables damping\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetLinearDamping()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsBody\fP setMass (number value)"

.PP
Set the body's mass\&. Scales inertia by newMass / oldMass, preserving a tuned inertia-to-mass ratio\&. Linear/angular velocity is unchanged, so momentum changes\&. Invalid or overflowing mass/inertia throws before changing state\&. NoPhysics ignores the operation\&.

.PP
For a \fBSprite\fP with an active explicit or generated animation physics rig, scales every registered component's mass/inertia while preserving their current proportions\&. A component edit changes only that body and consequently the total\&. The coordinating body adds no simulated mass\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvalue\fP Finite positive mass in your application's mass units\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetMass()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsBody\fP setMode (number value)"

.PP
Set the body's simulation mode\&. For ordinary bodies, switching out of dynamic mode clears forces\&. Static mode also clears linear and angular velocity\&. The absence value physicsBody_None cannot be assigned; remove the body from its owner instead\&. Invalid values throw on a present body\&. NoPhysics ignores the operation\&. Switching an owned body to dynamic mode cancels competing programmed movement/rotation tracks and rates while retaining size/appearance animation\&. A mounted \fBSprite\fP body must remain kinematic until detached\&.

.PP
Mapped animation bodies instead route through \fBSprite::setAnimationPhysicsMode()\fP: Dynamic releases rig tracking, Kinematic begins default 0\&.5-second recovery, and Static is rejected\&. Recovery reports a dynamic body until it reaches its target\&. This path preserves independent scheduled loads and rejects conflicting manual or \fBPart\fP IK drives until explicitly released\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvalue\fP One of \fR\fBpdg\&.physicsBody_Dynamic\fP\fP, \fR\fBpdg\&.physicsBody_Kinematic\fP\fP, or \fR\fBpdg\&.physicsBody_Static\fP\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetMode()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsBody\fP setMomentOfInertia (number value)"

.PP
Set the body's moment of inertia\&. Changes inertia without changing angular velocity\&. Visual resizing does not recalculate inertia\&. On an active rig, set inertia on each component; the coordinating \fBSprite\fP body rejects this setter\&. Invalid values throw on a present body\&. NoPhysics ignores the operation\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvalue\fP Finite positive rotational inertia in mass times distance squared\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetMomentOfInertia()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsBody\fP setRestitution (number value)"

.PP
Set the body's restitution\&. Controls bounce during contacts\&. It is independent of damping\&. Invalid values throw on a present body\&. NoPhysics ignores the operation\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvalue\fP Finite coefficient from 0 (inelastic) through 1 (fully elastic)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetRestitution()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsBody\fP setSpeed (number value)"

.PP
Set the body's speed\&. Preserves the current movement direction\&. A stationary body uses direction zero (positive x)\&. Static bodies retain zero velocity\&. Invalid values throw on a present body\&. NoPhysics ignores the operation\&.

